articles.content_en:
Article 18 Where any of the following circumstances occurs in violation of these Regulations, the competent department for supervision of ship breaking pollution shall, in addition to ordering correction within a specified time limit, also give a warning or impose a fine of not more than 10,000 yuan, depending on the circumstances:
(1) refusing or obstructing an on-site inspection by the competent department for supervision of ship breaking pollution, or practicing fraud during such inspection;
(2) failing to equip and use pollution prevention facilities, equipment, and appliances as required, thereby causing environmental pollution;
(3) taking measures to eliminate or control pollution after a pollution damage accident, but failing to report to the competent department for supervision of ship breaking pollution; or
(4) after the ship breaking unit is closed or relocated, the on-site cleanup of the original site fails to meet the requirements.
